  SO THE FIX IS AVAILABLE.  What it then has to explain is the AMOUNT, and there the ledger's own results bite:
     (1) NO STEP.  The required f = M_extra/M_b runs from 0.94 to 5.29 across 2.8 decades of enclosed baryonic mass, with d log f/d log M_b = -0.007 +- (scatter 0.239 dex).
         A free-streaming hot component must cluster MORE in deeper potentials -- f rising with mass.  The data give a slope of -0.007: it does not rise.  h55's own no-step result (-0.082 to +0.058 dex/dex in eta from 5e12 to 1.6e15) says the same thing from the other side.
     (2) THE WRONG SIGN IN REDSHIFT.  A component that clusters gravitationally has had LESS time to do so at high z, so f must FALL with redshift.  eRASS1 at fixed mass needs f = 2.22 at z ~ 0.1 and f = 3.96 at z ~ 0.85 -- it RISES by 78%.
